{
    "background_story": "Peanut was a small but feisty seagull who called the old pier his home. Every morning, he'd wake up to the sound of fishermen unloading their nets, and he'd swoop in to scavenge for scraps. The pier's weathered wooden beams were his playground, and he'd spend hours soaring above the water, playing a game of 'dodge the fishing rod'. Peanut's favorite pastime was watching the sunset over the ocean, when the pier would transform into a golden haven. He'd strut along the railing, feeling like the king of the coast. As the stars began to twinkle, Peanut would settle into his nest, a snug little bundle of twigs and feathers tucked away in a pier beam. He loved the pier's rustic charm and the sense of community that came with it \u2013 and the pier, in turn, loved having Peanut as its loyal resident mascot.",
